 **Outcome.** When the Implement-phase wave-dispatch step creates a stage commit labeled `merge(T20, T21, T22)`, the commit's actual git merge parents are validated to equal the expected full parent set captured at wave-dispatch resolution time — integration-base SHA plus the named task-tip SHAs. On mismatch, the wave halts with a named diagnostic and does not advance. The v0.7.2 self-host failure shape (a stage commit labeled `merge(task-21, task-26)` whose actual parents were `stage-after-W4` + `task-26-tip`, silently dropping all of task-21's work, including a security-relevant guard that shipped missing) cannot recur silently.
 
